  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 114 AM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nNorthwesterly flow aloft is forecast to continue across the\nregion through Friday. On Tuesday and Wednesday, high pressure\nis forecast to sit to the east of the area with southwesterly\nflow at the surface into the area. High temperatures on Tuesday\nand Wednesday will be noticeably warmer in the mid to upper 70s.\nTuesday is expected to be breezy with southwesterly winds of 10\nto 15 MPH and gusts up to 25 MPH. A subtle shortwave and cool \nfront is forecast to move across the region on Wednesday with no\nprecipitation expected. This results in cooler temperatures to \nend the work week. \n\nA subtle wave is forecast to move across the area Thursday\nnight into Friday morning resulting in a low confidence (10 to\n20%) chance of rain forecast for Thursday night into Friday \nmorning. The atmosphere moisture profiles remain dry and \nforcing is weak so any rainfall amounts would be very light. \n\nBy next weekend, ridging at the surface and aloft is forecast to\nbuild into the region ahead of a 500 MB trough in the Southern\nPlains. At this time, it looks like warm and dry weather will\nprevail through next weekend. Temperatures on Saturday will be 5\nto 10 degrees above normal with high temperatures both days in\nthe 70s. Both days will also be breezy with speeds of 10 to 15 \nMPH and gusts of 20 to 25 MPH.",
